'NO-COMPILE
' A FINAL flag read by a condition is the debug-switch antipattern. A rule whose behaviour
' depends on a flag takes it as a program parameter, where a test can set it.
' ERROR: always TRUE
' LINE: 10
PROGRAM P
    DECLARE big BOOLEAN FINAL = TRUE
    DECLARE n INTEGER
    n = 0
    IF big THEN
        n = 1
    END IF
    ASSERT "unreachable", n = 1
END.
